<title>ISRAEL: Israeli mutual funds' assets up in March.</title>
<headline>Israeli mutual funds' assets up in March.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1997-04-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Assets controlled by Israeli mutual funds in March rose to 15.39 billion shekels from 15.33 billion at the end of February, Meitav Investments and Securities said in a report on Sunday.</p>
<p>March was a month of profit-taking in the Tel Aviv stock market after months of sharp gains, Meitav said. This resulted in redemptions of 150 million shekels from funds investing in stocks, offset by deposits totalling 173 million shekels in funds investing in unlinked bonds.</p>
<p>($1=3.36 shekels)</p>
<p>- Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211</p>
